WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.913
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.090
- Good morning guys.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.680
The first video I ever
uploaded to YouTube,

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.880
was my morning routine

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.510
and you turned it into a smash hit.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:16.920
Now, a lot has changed in my life

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.050
within the last year.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.550
I have my new puppy Bear,

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:20.930
I finished my residency

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.270
and I'm practicing as a
Board-Certified doctor.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:26.193
So I decided to give you
my updated morning routine

00:00:26.193 --> 00:00:28.960
with the help of my new
Lenovo Smart Display,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.080
with the Google Assistant.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.330
Shout out to Lenovo, for
sponsoring this video.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.163
Let's get started.

00:00:33.163 --> 00:00:35.500
My mornings often start very early

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.260
with the alarm clock ringing

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.430
and really taking me out of a deep sleep.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.020
Don't hit that snooze button.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.470
It's gonna make you feel groggy

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.500
and make it even harder
to wake up in the morning.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.116
The first thing that I
do once I get out of bed

00:00:46.116 --> 00:00:47.930
is open the shades.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:49.570
You want that natural light hitting you

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:50.930
as soon as you wake up.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:53.400
Not only does it make it
easier for you to wake up

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.480
but it also resets your circadian rhythms

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.390
so you can fall asleep easier at night.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.050
Next, I make my bed.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.710
Now this hasn't changed from
my previous morning routine

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:02.700
and for good reason.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.658
Both psych and military experts alike

00:01:04.658 --> 00:01:06.720
recommend making your bed.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.960
It yields tremendous productivity

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.240
and willpower benefits throughout the day.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.130
Once my bed is all done,
I go on to brush my teeth.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.850
You should be doing this twice a day,

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.420
and not only is it important
for your dental health,

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.850
but we've seen relationships
between heart disease

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.710
and those who don't take
care of their teeth.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:26.130
Something I know a lot of
people skip out on is flossing.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.070
Now I have braces in the back of my teeth,

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.610
so it's not so easy to floss,

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.410
but I use a Waterpik flosser.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.270
It does the same job, shooting out

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.870
a high speed stream of water,

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.040
getting that gunk out
from in between my teeth.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.189
Hey Google, good morning.

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:39.930
- [Google Assistant]
Good morning Doctor Mike.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.370
It is 7:02am.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.580
Today it'll be cloudy with
a forecasted high of 69

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.700
and a low of 59.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.647
- Gonna be cold.

00:01:46.647 --> 00:01:47.480
- [Google Assistant] By the way,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.900
you need to film YouTube morning routine.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.400
Also, don't forget to go to your meeting.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.420
- The Lenovo Smart Display
with Google Assistant

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.330
has my entire schedule in it.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:00.970
It has my reminders, the weather
updates, traffic updates.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.530
In the morning when you're tired,

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:04.690
and you need your routine to be on point,

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.690
this thing has it all in one place.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:07.960
Wait, where's Bear?

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.954
Hey, hey puppy.

00:02:09.954 --> 00:02:11.006
Good morning little Bear.

00:02:11.006 --> 00:02:11.923
I love you.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:15.760
Good morning, good boy.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.260
Yeah, good morning.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.730
I know Bear, I feel the same way.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:19.563
You ready to eat?

00:02:19.563 --> 00:02:20.396
Who's ready to eat?

00:02:20.396 --> 00:02:21.860
This is my morning routine right here.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.280
Shower with the dog,

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.695
and then shower in the
bathroom afterwards.

00:02:25.695 --> 00:02:27.803
Good boy. Yeah.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.910
(dog chewing)

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:37.300
So, Bear ate, and clearly he's happy,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.210
but I didn't eat.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.110
Generally I'll go for some oatmeal,

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.958
but I'm not afraid of
doing intermittent fasting.

00:02:42.958 --> 00:02:45.548
Sometimes I wake up, I don't
have much of an appetite,

00:02:45.548 --> 00:02:47.200
I do intermittent fast,

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.340
but let's get the Lenovo smart assistant,

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:51.410
powered by Google, to
help us out this morning.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.847
Hey Google, show me a recipe for oatmeal.

00:02:53.847 --> 00:02:55.813
- [Google Assistant]
Here are some recipes.

00:03:01.258 --> 00:03:02.297
- Ah, hot.

00:03:02.297 --> 00:03:03.413
Smells good though.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.020
The reason you see me put so
many fruits into my oatmeal,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.800
is because I want it to taste good

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.200
and instead of putting sweeteners in,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.760
I'd rather just put in more fruits

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.510
because if fruits
vitamins, minerals, fiber

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.010
so you don't absorb as
readily all of the sugars,

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.030
I think that's the best way to do it.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.720
Mm, that's really good.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.790
Want a bite?

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.690
Bear wants a bite.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.600
But Bear wants a bite of anything.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.470
I take Bear on a walk every morning,

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.400
somewhere around 15, 20 minutes.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.840
He needs a nice long walk,

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.130
so that when he's at home
during the day alone,

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.700
he doesn't destroy the entire house.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:37.190
That's a mistake I see people make a lot.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.510
If you saw my previous
morning routine video,

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.350
I was doing some
calisthenics in the morning.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:43.580
Now, I got this stationary bike,

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.730
so I'm cycling pretty much every morning.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.750
Get to do like 20, 30 minutes
of solid interval training

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.730
so my heart rate gets
better, burn some calories,

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.120
keep the weight off, all
without losing muscle.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.210
I always tell my patients,

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.345
you don't need to spend
a lot of time exercising

00:03:57.345 --> 00:03:58.913
in order to lose weight.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.540
One thing I have to do
every morning is do my hair.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.890
As you saw earlier in the
video, my hair's a mess

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:06.830
when I wake up.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:09.440
The only way I can get it
normal is through blow drying.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.210
I use a little heat protecting spray

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.700
just because I'm blow
drying my hair very often.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.590
And then, I let the blow
dryer let the magic happen.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.731
And a simple round brush.

00:04:17.731 --> 00:04:20.814
(hair dryer blowing)

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:24.370
Keeping it simple, get
a little hair product,

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:27.100
clay or pomade, whatever you like using

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.650
and then let it work its magic.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.090
Every morning, before I set out to work,

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:37.940
I like to sit right here on this couch

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:40.340
for like five minutes, just focusing,

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.950
and I know a lot of successful
people like to meditate,

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:44.900
but this isn't about sitting cross-legged

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:46.280
with your fingers touching.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.770
This is about being mindful.

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:50.330
Thinking about what's in your unconscious.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:51.340
I know that sounds deep,

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:52.559
but it's really about thinking about

00:04:52.559 --> 00:04:54.550
what emotions are you feeling?

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:56.010
What are you feeling them about?

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.220
What's bothering you?

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.770
And when you connect those feelings

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.570
and you're true about how you feel,

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.490
you can be so much more
productive throughout your day.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:04.940
I've definitely noticed a benefit,

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.700
and it's something I
recommend to you at home.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.490
Now I need to get dressed for work

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.660
and depending on where
I'm working that day,

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.310
I have to put on a different outfit.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:14.930
For example, if I'm going
on TV to do the news,

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:17.100
I have to put on the full suit and tie.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:19.470
If I'm gonna be working
the hospital that day,

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.820
I put on slacks, dress shirt, tie

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.130
and then finally, if I'm
working the urgent care,

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.100
I throw on my scrubs,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.070
'cause I don't want to
get my own clothes dirty.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.230
I think it's really important
that you feel comfortable

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:31.370
in what you're wearing because it shows.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:32.620
You become more comfortable

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.220
and when you dress like a professional,

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:35.970
you get treated like a professional.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:37.670
Time to go to the hospital, but first,

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.880
let me check the traffic.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.070
Hey Google, what's traffic
like going to work?

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.300
- [Google Assistant] On your way to work,

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:43.900
